It is Friday evening.
Anitha comes to my flat.
Her dog Tommy is with her.
She gives me his food and leash.
She explains some rules to me.
"Maya, you must feed him at eight o'clock in the morning," Anitha says.
"You must give dinner at seven o'clock in the evening."
"You must not give him any other food."
"He likes sweet snacks very much."
"But you absolutely must not give him sweet things."
"It is very bad for him."
"Also, you must not let him out alone."
"When going out, you must always watch him."
I tell Anitha: "Do not worry, Anitha."
"I will look after him well."
Anitha happily says goodbye and leaves.
I close the door.
"Come here, Tommy," I call him.
